{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/98557","id":2147314123,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc5__WnL","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98557","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98557.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98557.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98557","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/98557/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/98557/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98557/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/15d6657dbcc98ccd0fd9ecee21a565d705526f76","number":98557,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"GDScript: Implement soft access restriction for members prefixed with `_` and `__` (as warning by default)","user":{"login":"Lazy-Rabbit-2001","id":22123964,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMTIzOTY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22123964?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001","html_url":"https://github.com/Lazy-Rabbit-2001","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Supersedes: #98136\r\nCloses: https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/641\r\n\r\nAfter the discussion with some devs, with the philosophy of \"implementing new features without game crashing\". Here is the temporary discussion result **in my opinion**:  \r\n\r\nRather than keywords and annotations, it's better to keep the original form that `_` as prefix of private/protected members. There are three reasons for that:\r\n\r\n# Reasons\r\n\r\n1. Based on @HolonProduction and KaiN's opinions, a virutal method should be **private or protected**, but normally it is protected, so a virtual method that begins with `_` should be a *protected* method. At first, I thought this would be redundant, until the moment I imagined encapsulation on calling a custom virtual method:\r\n```GDScript\r\nfunc _custom_virtual():\r\n    <contents>\r\n\r\n## Wrapper and encapsulator function to call the custom virtual method:\r\nfunc call_custom_virtual():\r\n    <some preparations related to the virtual method>\r\n    _custom_virtual()\r\n```\r\nWhen you need to call a custom virtual method, it is better to call it through a wrapper.\r\n2. From the perspective of technical reasons, `private` and `protect` need to do checks during the reduction. The original pr did checks by retracing the source `GDScriptParser::Node`, and even to retrace not only its super classes, but also the head attributes, which is much more performance-costly. However, by operating on `p_identifier->name`, we do not need to trace back what its `GDScriptParser::Node` is and where it comes from; Instead, we just check if the class or the super classes has the member or the method. For protected identifiers, we just iterate the super classes of `parser->current_class`, which greatly reduces the consumption of CPU performance. Compared with the implementation of original pr, this is of balanced cost.\r\n3. Based on the philosophy of \"implementing new features without crashing the games\", I turned the error into a warning. Of course you can turn it back to an error in GDScript warning settings. However, due to the fact that this pr is merely a soft implementation of access restriction, this does not break the runtime or throw an error if there is any invalid interclass access, so if your game runs out of your expectation, it's time to check your code, especially maybe somewhere you referenced a `_`-prefixed variable?\r\n\r\n# Implementation effect\r\n\r\nWhen you trying to access a `_`-prefixed (or `__`-prefixed) identifier outside the class that defines it, a warning (by default) will be thrown at the bottom of the script editor about trying accessing a private/protected member externally.\r\n\r\n**Note:** For attributes, this also take the invalid ones into consideration, e.g.:\r\n\r\n```GDScript\r\nclass A:\r\n    var _test = 1\r\n\r\nclass B:\r\n    var a = A.new()\r\n\r\n    func _init():\r\n        a._tet = 2 # This is, in fact, an invalid attribute and may cause runtime error. However, this would be considered as warning of accessing private/protected member externally as well.\r\n````\r\n\r\nFor protected members, this warning would be eliminated if the accessor class is derived from the class where the target identifier is declared.\r\n\r\n# Discussions\r\n\r\nI know that this would bring to thumbups from those who think this is correct, or thumbdowns from those who think that I'm standing for official devs. No matter what this post will be given with, feel free to share and discuss your ideas here.\r\n\r\n# Plans\r\n- [x] ~~Distinguishing color for `_`-or-`__`-prefixed members in auto-completion.~~(Off-topic)\r\n- [x] ~~Distinguishing color for `_`-or-`__`-prefixed exported members in the editor inspector.~~(Off-topic)\r\n- [x] ~~Introducing `__` as the prefix of protected members (or private ones, needs to be discussed)~~ I implement this before the For protected identifiers, we just iterate the super classes of `parser->current_class`. discussion on this. If this is no more needed, I'll remove this feature.\r\n- [x] Unit tests for members prefixed with `_` and `__`.\r\n- [ ] Peer reviews and tests.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":73330068,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2OA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/feature%20proposal","name":"feature proposal","description":"","color":"4466ff","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097162,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTcxNjI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/discussion","name":"discussion","description":"","color":"ccaaff","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098082,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgwODI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:gdscript","name":"topic:gdscript","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2024-10-26T15:20:14Z","updated_at":"2025-03-12T01:56:48Z","closed_at":"2025-03-07T11:54:47Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"9aa03a332bb0657bd43a5aa5fef6379d77da55b1","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonPr